{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.72,"content_digest":"692800436b88deabc2b08468975ea76440f10bddc2516dfca3fdfdb988ce72f1","created_at":"2026-08-22T03:36:40+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[],"link_id":"foundation-link:7a0854fbf857d123e6273770","meta_principle_id":"meta:scientific-discovery:scientific-memory-negative-results","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:general:01KZZYNY0V7CT3J9C5Y6CH8E3X","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The meta-principle that discovery systems must preserve failed tests and counterexamples as first-class knowledge directly supports the claim that full experiment history improves feature-selection consistency and reduces repeated low-value proposals. The claim is an empirical instance of preserving search history to avoid rediscovering failures.","relation_type":"supports","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-22T04:12:58+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0KTQZ6M68SKHPKARZR7EKFP"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T03:36:40+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"partial","confidence":0.55,"content_digest":"2a16d64d15783b0c82cb9a022911f848719895b391de88f3205f409f8014b4c2","created_at":"2026-08-23T04:40:53+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"6024648b5a20e1670e53790d19bd2378a8223f70228b4942c0583ce51ba92ee7","input_tokens":5783,"latency_ms":31249,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"1bb65d2a9c764fa2487e5764ab929836c1d656d485a41788fd98d33ea2fd6a8a","output_tokens":2483,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:9fbda4d5397fbe0ca6075c1e","meta_principle_id":"meta:scientific-discovery:active-learning","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:biology-evolution:01M0PEPW7NS9H8VDGPX1ZWCWEG","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The principle's use of prediction deviation to select experiments in a partially observed model is a specific instance of uncertainty-guided adaptive measurement, which is the core idea of active learning. The reported reduction of uncertainty over a sequence is consistent with active learning's expected behavior, though the empirical result is study-bound and not entailed by the meta-principle.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T08:08:08+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0PTK9G6V6VXNVFWAWBHMSYT"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T04:40:53+00:00","variable_compatibility":"partial"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.8,"content_digest":"d33c47a6c87b3fa339f16183b04fad693239c36d773c975dd4d402e35f56788d","created_at":"2026-08-23T13:01:15+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"9b936ba3ee1d65152a184201d125e297b70343c64eefa5bb0d997fac9e8e3d2a","input_tokens":5709,"latency_ms":48170,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"6061a29b1de7087a8dcf7908ab5e80d5aaaf34afae7458c2f5dde5e138d7a213","output_tokens":2665,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:a1a576a37a147429e1cfbd99","meta_principle_id":"meta:scientific-discovery:bayesian-experimental-design","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0QBAHB6BSMH9E70BX9VMXCK","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"Bayesian experimental design ranks experiments by expected information gain and emphasizes asking the most discriminating question. The target principle explains why exhaustive within-regime testing can have low discrimination value when hypotheses agree locally but diverge globally, so it supports the design principle's motivation to seek experiments that distinguish globally divergent alternatives.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T13:01:15+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.62,"content_digest":"fcc5a5a0364f603f7f36b38e79b14e51e9e2e8240ff665dc9286bc04c6adf065","created_at":"2026-08-23T11:03:28+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"1285256814f494e2bbc2a3680804bbc983f62cb2f86e099b3681c994fcca93e0","input_tokens":5958,"latency_ms":30632,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"b975dd937b21391c2e3a93e0aeddaf50137f7cf454c221f0642ee3abc87e8334","output_tokens":2421,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:b39456bb6aee8b2c97c957d0","meta_principle_id":"meta:chemistry-materials:defects-and-metastability","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:scientific-discovery:01M0Q4KD0PHCF4JQ9YMH6M75S4","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The borophene stability observation involves adatoms and intercalated-ion removal, i.e. defect/guest states that can dominate real material behavior. The meta-principle provides a broad materials context for why such non-ideal configurations matter, while the specific AIMD stability result remains an independent empirical finding.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T11:03:28+00:00","variable_compatibility":"partial"}
